<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			19/6/97		  12/6/97	     23/6/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    450		  425-450		   350</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75		   75-100		 50-75</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,800		    1,900		 1,350</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	300-325		  275-300	     275-300</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15		    15-20		  5-10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose as incoming barges and cargoes offset quietish outgoing material to Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks fell on a lack of incoming product for the second week going and the depature of product into Germany for use in the chemical sector.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks slipped as outgoing barrels into Switzerland, Germany, Benelux and France offset incoming material.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose on the back of incoming straight-run and slowish bunker offtake while jet slipped a touch as material headed into the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
